WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.000
PROLOGUE — SRI MAHA VISHNU: When Dharma Falls

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.500
Before the dawn of creation, Sri Maha Vishnu rested upon Ananta in eternal contemplation.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:12.800
Whenever dharma fades, Maha Vishnu descends.

00:00:13.199 --> 00:00:19.500
I — MATSYA: When furious waters dissolved the earth, Matsya guided the sacred boat, preserving life and eternal wisdom.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:28.500
II — KURMA: As gods and demons churned the cosmic ocean, Kurma bore Mount Mandara upon His back to steady creation.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:37.500
III — VARAHA: Plunging into the dark primal abyss, Varaha lifted Mother Earth upon His tusks, restoring Her to eternal light.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:46.500
IV — NARASIMHA: Bursting from the shattered pillar, fierce Narasimha destroyed demonic arrogance and shielded unwavering devotion.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:55.500
V — VAMANA: Measuring the universe in three cosmic strides, Vamana taught that true humility surpasses all power.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:04.500
VI — PARASHURAMA: Wielding the sacred battle-axe, Parashurama punished corrupt tyranny and decreed power must obey dharma.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:13.500
VII — RAMA: Mariyada Purushottama Sri Rama sacrificed all worldly comfort, demonstrating righteousness must triumph at any cost.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:22.500
VIII — KRISHNA: On the battlefield of Kurukshetra, Krishna unveiled the Bhagavad Gita—the immortal beacon of wisdom.

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:31.500
IX — BUDDHA: Forsaking the illusions of power and war, Buddha illuminated the path of profound peace and compassion.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:40.500
X — KALKI: Riding the blazing white steed Devadatta, Kalki descends to conquer darkness and herald the golden dawn.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:50.500
FINALE: Ten divine descents across the cosmic wheel of time. The promise remains eternal: Dharma will rise. Om Namo Narayanaya.

